  "docs": {
    "readme": {
      "path": "Synapse-itf-Dev/README.md",
      "title": "Synapse-ITF-Dev",
      "excerpt": "# Synapse-ITF-Dev\n\nGit-integrated source repository for the **ITF FROG** Azure Synapse Analytics workspace (`vwag-frog-itf-dev-syn-ws`, workspace factory identity `testfrog`). It contains the full ARM/Synapse-native artifact set (pipelines, dataflows, datasets, linked services, notebooks, SQL scripts, triggers) used to build and deploy the ITF FROG ETL/reporting solution across environments via Azure DevOps/Synapse \"Publish\".\n\n> See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for a history of workspace changes and instructions on how to log new ones.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe workspace implements an end-to-end ETL pipeline for **ITF (Adastra/PLBM/PAF Finance) & SharePoint** source data into a Synapse dedicated SQL Pool (`itf_frog`), which is then exposed for reporting (Power BI).\n\nThis repository owns the Synapse application and data-platform artifacts, not the Azure platform itself. [`itf-frog-infra`](../itf-frog-infra/README.md) provisions the workspaces, storage, networking, Key Vault, pools and monitoring. [`itf-frog-devops`](../itf-frog-devops/README.md) checks out this repository, applies environment-specific parameters, deploys the artifacts and SQL objects, approves managed private endpoints, and promotes releases from QS to Prod. The operational dependency is: **infrastructure first -> artifact deployment second -> scheduled Synapse processing**.\n\nTwo independent data domains are orchestrated:\n\n1. **Adastra / PLBM datalake ETL** – Raw files are copied from an Adastra file share into ADLS Gen2, promoted through **Landing → Curated → Staging** using PySpark notebooks on a Synapse Spark pool, then loaded into the SQL Pool through **Core** (staging → core) and **Reporting** (core → reporting) stored-procedure driven stages.\n2. **SharePoint Excel ETL** – Excel-based SharePoint lists/files (`DS_Excel_SharePointData`) are ingested directly into SQL Pool tables via 8 parallel mapping data flows (`DF_sharepoint_Prod_01`–`08`).\n\nA third set of pipelines manages the **compute lifecycle of the dedicated SQL Pool** (scale up before business hours, scale down / pause after hours) to control cost.\n\nAll stages include structured error handling: failures are captured with `SetVariable`/`Switch` activities and persisted to SQL Pool logging tables (`dwh.sp_log_error`, `dbo.usp_SpDFMasterLogPipelineError`) for auditability.\n\n## Repository / Folder Structure\n\nThis follows the standard Synapse workspace Git-export layout — every folder maps 1:1 to a Synapse artifact type:\n\n| Folder | Content"
    },
